From 3fbeed7afbb6f520312c6bd3fb56ee73b4a50332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "xuan.huang" <5563315+Huxpro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:50:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(motion): support easing callbacks in declarative
 transitions

Transitions reach the main thread as JSON, which drops easing callbacks and
turns Infinity into null. Encode both in one place: easing callbacks are
sampled into a piecewise-linear table and rebuilt on the main thread, and
repeat: Infinity is preserved at every transition level. Also bind the base
animate completion dispatcher while the worklet is executing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
